```js
function kaunter() {
  let n = 0;
  return () => ++n;
}
const c = kaunter();
console.log(c(), c()); // 1 2
```
The inner function keeps `n` alive after `kaunter` returns — true privacy without classes. Classic leak source: closures capturing big objects in long-lived handlers.

```js
const { nama, umur = 0 } = pengguna;
const [pertama, ...lain] = senarai;
const salin = { ...asal, umur: 21 };
```
Destructure function params for self-documenting signatures; spread copies shallowly (nested objects still shared — use structuredClone for deep). Rest collects leftovers in both arrays and objects.

```js
// util.js
export const tambah = (a, b) => a + b;
export default function utama() {}
// guna:
import utama, { tambah } from "./util.js";
```
Named exports refactor safely (IDE renames all sites) and tree-shake; default exports hide names. Prefer named; one default per module max, and always include the `.js` extension in ESM import paths.
